course: dictionary
lesson: 12272
title: Continuously: without a break
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Continuously means without stopping, or all the time over a long period. When you meet it, ask: did something keep going with no break? «The tap dripped continuously all night.» The tap never stopped, so the water dripped without a break.
explain: Continuously is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. «The machine ran continuously for three days.» Ran how? Continuously, which means it never stopped. Use the swap test: put "without stopping" in its place. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Continuously does not mean "now and then". A doorbell rings from time to time, but a clock ticks continuously, with no gaps at all. Look for clues like all night, for days, or over a long time, because they show that something lasts without a break.
fact: Continuously means without stopping or without a break.
fact: Continuously can also mean all the time, again and again, over a long period.
fact: «The tap dripped continuously» means the water never stopped, so a dripping tap wastes a lot of water.
fact: In maths, «a car moving continuously at 60 km/h» keeps the same speed the whole time, so you can use distance = speed × time.
fact: Useful phrases: run continuously, continuously changing, continuously improving.
exercise: «The fridge hummed continuously all night.» What does continuously mean here? | Now and then, with long gaps | Only once | Very quietly | *Without stopping
exercise: «The car travelled continuously at 60 km/h.» In maths, what does this tell you? | The car was going slower and slower | *The car kept the same speed the whole time | The car stopped for a rest every hour | The car was painted red
exercise: Ella says, «Her reading is continuously improving.» What does this mean? | She is reading only on Tuesdays | *She gets better all the time | She reads a book once in a while | She stopped reading last year
test: «The alarm rang continuously until someone switched it off.» What does continuously mean? | *It rang without stopping | It rang backwards | It rang once and then went quiet | It rang with breaks in between
test: Which sentence shows something that keeps changing all the time? | The leaves fell once in autumn | *The weather is continuously changing | The door was shut at six | The cake was baked yesterday
exam: Sam says continuously is the same as "once in a while". Is he right? | Yes, both mean rarely | *No, continuously means without a break or all the time | No, continuously means very loudly | Yes, both mean very fast
